"}, {"type": "skill", "content": "Speaking"}], "type": "learning_skills"}], "questions": [{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "pdf", "content": "enpe8n7le01ob02re7pdf01.pdf"}], "type": "question"}], "responses": [{"_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "selected": 0, "correct": 1, "id": 0}], "id": 0}], "type": "DWS", "template_override": 1, "id": 11}], "stimuli": [{"_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}], "type": "welcome", "template_override": 1}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n7le01ob02re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob02re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "Choosing an ideal IT contract should not be brought about too soon. It is necessary to emphasize on the importance of selecting a contract in which the terms are well defined and appropriate for a project.\nA first recommendation when negotiating IT contractual terms is to retain counsel specialized in IT contract law, which is not inexpensive but it can be worth the cost in the case of contract disputes in the future. Additionally, a second recommendation is not to force working relationships. If agreement or a primary goal is not achieved, it might be a hint of what the relationship is going to be like."}, {"time": "38500", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob02re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "At the outset of an IT negotiation, some contract deliverables of interest for both parties in an IT contract should be taken into account. The contract must ensure that the terms and conditions that are included in it are balanced. They also have to make sure that the definition of the course of action for both parties, and an agreeable and reliable working relationship are achieved after the negotiation."}, {"time": "64000", "image": "enpe8n7le01ob02re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "Now that the groundwork has been discussed, let's list the most common key areas to nearly all IT software contracts:\nSoftware, which summarizes the actual aspects of the IT product that is procured; hardware, which includes all the hardware specifications and requirements; professional services, which mention the expected tasks and services of IT consultants; training, which includes characteristics and conditions related to all software training aspects; implementation scope, which relates to the project charter, objectives schedule and detailed assumptions; and general terms and conditions, which gives an all-inclusive summary of the main aspects in the contract.\nThis list is not intended to be complete, but it does mention some aspects that are not always taken into account when establishing contractual terms."}], "coverimg": "enpe8n7le01ob02re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "type": "scholar"}]}